    },
    {
      "sourceAlias": "L0836:S0",
      "page": 21,
      "pageStratum": "SEEDED_INTERIOR",
      "text": "that they form a list of m nondecreasing integers of log m bits each. We will store the differences",
      "label": "OTHER",
      "goldStatus": "LABELED"
    },
    {
      "sourceAlias": "L0837:S0",
      "page": 21,
      "pageStratum": "SEEDED_INTERIOR",
      "text": "between consecutive integers in the list, in unary encoding: difference δi = pi − pi−1, where pi is the",
      "label": "OTHER",
      "goldStatus": "LABELED"
    },
    {
      "sourceAlias": "L0838:S0",
      "page": 21,
      "pageStratum": "SEEDED_INTERIOR",
      "text": "i-th prefix, is encoded as 0δi1 (i.e. δi occurrences of bit ’0’ followed by one bit ’1’). For example, the",
      "label": "OTHER",
      "goldStatus": "LABELED"
    },
    {
      "sourceAlias": "L0839:S0",
      "page": 21,
      "pageStratum": "SEEDED_INTERIOR",
      "text": "difference δ8 between the two adjacent prefixes p7 = 101 and p8 = 111 is (111 − 101)2 = 2; we encode",
      "label": "OTHER",
      "goldStatus": "LABELED"
    },
    {
      "sourceAlias": "L0840:S0",
      "page": 21,
      "pageStratum": "SEEDED_INTERIOR",
      "text": "this difference as δ8 = 021 = 001. The first difference is defined as δ1 = p1. The concatenated bits of",
      "label": "OTHER",
      "goldStatus": "LABELED"
    },
    {
      "sourceAlias": "L0841:S0",
      "page": 21,
      "pageStratum": "SEEDED_INTERIOR",
      "text": "this encoding of δ1,...,δm is the second part EF2 of the EF data structure:",
